WEBVTT

NOTE week07-clip3-med-palm-m
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.249 line:2 align:center
CLIP can score how well each
caption fits a chest X-ray,

2
00:00:04.249 --> 00:00:07.406 line:2 align:center
but it can only choose
among captions we give it.

3
00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:11.550 line:2 align:center
A radiology report has to
be written, word by word.

4
00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.835 line:2 align:center
So we feed the image
into a language model.

5
00:00:14.835 --> 00:00:20.649 line:2 align:center
A vision transformer cuts the X-ray into
patches and turns each one into a vector.

6
00:00:20.649 --> 00:00:27.150 line:2 align:center
A projection then resizes these vectors
to the size of the model's word tokens.

7
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:30.917 line:2 align:center
The image tokens go in
front of the instruction,

8
00:00:30.917 --> 00:00:33.085 line:2 align:center
write the findings for this X-ray,

9
00:00:33.085 --> 00:00:39.164 line:2 align:center
and the whole sequence enters the same
decoder we saw in weeks four and five.

10
00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:42.883 line:2 align:center
It writes the report one token at a time.

11
00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:49.064 line:2 align:center
Training uses the same next-token loss
as supervised fine-tuning in week five.

12
00:00:49.064 --> 00:00:56.017 line:2 align:center
It is counted only on the report tokens,
not on the image or the instruction.

13
00:00:56.217 --> 00:00:58.241 line:2 align:center
Med-PaLM M starts from PaLM-E,

14
00:00:58.241 --> 00:01:02.005 line:2 align:center
a Palm language model joined
to a vision transformer,

15
00:01:02.005 --> 00:01:06.759 line:2 align:center
in sizes from 12 billion
to 562 billion parameters.

16
00:01:06.759 --> 00:01:11.334 line:2 align:center
It is fine-tuned on 14
tasks across 7 modalities,

17
00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:14.683 line:2 align:center
with one set of weights for all of them.

18
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:20.348 line:2 align:center
On 246 chest X-rays, clinicians
preferred Med-PaLM M's report

19
00:01:20.348 --> 00:01:27.322 line:2 align:center
to the radiologist's in up to 40.5% of
cases. Without any training examples,

20
00:01:27.322 --> 00:01:31.875 line:2 align:center
it detected tuberculosis
with 87.7% accuracy,

21
00:01:31.875 --> 00:01:36.417 line:2 align:center
against 92.6 for a specialist model.

22
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:41.811 line:2 align:center
But this was a side-by-side ranking
of past cases, not use in the clinic,

23
00:01:41.811 --> 00:01:46.736 line:2 align:center
and in most cases the model's
report was not the one preferred.

24
00:01:46.736 --> 00:01:52.147 line:2 align:center
We return to evaluation
and deployment in week 12.
